    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "There's now an informational message in dev (similar to what we have for `preserveSharedStateOnUnmount`).\r\n\r\nOn updating examples, there's still the particular case of `routing: true` which I've left as-is. This means they will still write on dispose, and show a message on the console. I've chosen not to update them as I think explicitly adding the router with the option clashes with the simplicity of this approach, and users will still have to learn about the change in behaviour in migration notes / codemods for next major version.",
    "commit_id": "f82e3d5f8af55f8a0e05f5d5f6cd78d264b20766",
    "created_at": "2023-12-18T13:50:16Z",
